gl-stereo (0.4.4-1) testing; urgency=medium

  * gl-stereo-savers depends on the exact XScreenSaver build its receipts name:
    the packages that own the saver executables and settings files the 132
    receipts bind, each (= its version), written into the Depends at build
    time from the files install-qualified.py just proved equal. An
    XScreenSaver rebuild can no longer be paired with receipts proved on
    another one (0.4.2 offered 1 of 132 savers against +stereo3d4+lc1).
  * A saver the catalogue cannot offer is said, never just left out: the
    controller's log and `catalogue.py CATALOGUE` name each one with the
    differing file and both hashes, and the saver list shows "Not offered"
    with the reason and a count, in the nine languages (German added to the
    list's strings). Receipts also bind each saver's settings file now.
  * install-qualified.py names every receipt whose layer or saver binary is
    not the installed one, with both hashes, instead of the first id.
  * New packaging/check-round-savers.py, the publication gate: a round whose
    gl-stereo-savers would offer fewer savers than it ships against that
    round's XScreenSaver, or does not pin it exactly, is refused. New test
    tests/saver-receipts.py (red and green on synthetic rounds).
  * No change to the layer or to how any saver draws.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:51:38 -0300

gl-stereo (0.4.3-1) testing; urgency=medium

  * X11: say it when the compositor did not double a declared window within
    the wait, instead of leaving a black second view that looks like success.
    The wait is GL_STEREO_DOUBLING_WAIT_MS (1000 by default, 0 or
    GL_STEREO_NO_DOUBLING_WAIT does not wait).
  * New tests/nvidia-rig: the proof rig of the two NVIDIA OpenGL paths (an SDL
    stereo window and a Qt stereo widget with the colours of each eye, the
    capture check, one fresh KWin session per probe, loops with a control).
  * The 130 screensaver receipts are requalified for this layer, from fresh
    installed-file sweeps of the savers of xscreensaver 6.09+dfsg1-2+stereo3d4+lc1
    (118 layer, 10 flat, 2 owning-fix receipts; the gates are those of 0.4.2).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 15:21:52 -0300

gl-stereo (0.4.2-1) testing; urgency=medium

  * Every OpenGL 4.6 drawing command reaches the view it names: the
    instanced draws with a base instance, multi-draw with a base vertex,
    the indirect draws with a count from a buffer and the transform
    feedback draws were drawn once into the left view, so Blender's right
    eye on NVIDIA's own OpenGL showed only its menus and panels. New test
    tests/draw-commands, also in the installed tests.
  * gl-stereo-savers depends on xscreensaver 6.09+dfsg1-2+stereo3d3, whose
    glsnake no longer lights its scene from uninitialised memory and lets
    the user choose its second light (glsnake's receipt is an owning fix).
  * The 130 screensaver receipts are requalified for the new layer by an
    audit whose checks give the same answer on any machine (fixed address
    layout, FlipText's frame 1000, captures after KWin sizes the window,
    synthetic Mapscroller tiles with the network off) and a new gate on
    the mean depth residual of all depth receipts.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:58:27 -0300

gl-stereo (0.4.1-1) testing; urgency=medium

  * The build's screensaver checks wait for what they test, a saver's
    selected frame, a frame from its stream or its exit, up to
    GL_STEREO_TEST_SECONDS (60 by default), instead of fixed waits of three
    to eight seconds that a loaded build machine could miss. The layer and
    the savers are unchanged.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0300

gl-stereo (0.4.0-1) testing; urgency=medium

  * Provide two views where the driver has none: on native Wayland,
    EGL_EXT_multiview_window with a buffer twice the window's width,
    declared full side by side (kde_stereo_content_v1 version 2), beside
    the GLX quad-buffer configs on X11. OpenGL ES contexts name the views
    through GL_EXT_multiview_draw_buffers.
  * X11: wait for the compositor to double a declared window before the
    driver sizes its buffers; NVIDIA's OpenGL intermittently left the
    second view black.
  * Leave a program's own two views to a driver that has them: Mesa's EGL
    on Wayland, and on X11 with GL_STEREO_DRIVER_VIEWS=1, which
    gl-stereo-run sets; the layer alone keeps the X11 packing, which its
    frame stream needs.
  * X11: tell a doubled window by its observed size, set a context's first
    viewport to the window's logical size, recognise stereo visuals by ID.
  * Leave the fixed-function state alone in core profile, forward-compatible
    and OpenGL ES contexts (Magnum gave up at start), and follow the eye a
    program chooses through direct state access on the window's
    framebuffer.
  * Receipts for all 130 savers with this layer, from fresh installed-file
    sweeps; the requalification tools ship in the source.
  * gl-stereo-run: on NVIDIA, choose Mesa on NVIDIA's Vulkan (zink, the
    default) or NVIDIA's own OpenGL; the dialog in nine languages. The
    choice applies when NVIDIA's OpenGL serves the display.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:40:01 -0300

gl-stereo (0.3.0-1) testing; urgency=medium

  * Extend camera recognition to shader uniforms and combined matrix forms.
  * Preserve per-eye camera textures and resolve multisample CPU captures.
  * Add the complete saver chooser with persistent rotation preferences.
  * Ship binary-bound qualification for all 130 OpenGL savers, plus Starfield
    and Rocks; require the XScreenSaver build with Flurry camera exposure.

